---
import Layout from "@layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="What Tailwind Asylum is for and how the blog section is organised."
>
	<p class="mb-3 text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide text-accent uppercase">About</p>
	<h1 class="font-display max-w-[16ch] text-3xl font-semibold sm:text-4xl">What this repo is for.</h1>

	<div class="prose dark:prose-invert mt-8 max-w-none">
		<p>
			<strong>Tailwind Asylum</strong> is a runnable Astro, Tailwind CSS, and React site used for examples,
			support cases, bug reproductions, and design tests. It is boilerplate, not a product &mdash;
			<code>main</code> stays clean and reusable so it can be reused for whatever comes up next.
		</p>
		<p>
			Each entry in the <a href="/asylum/">blog section</a> is a self-contained case: a short write-up
			paired with an editable HTML/CSS/JS playground powered by Sandpack, so a reported bug or design
			question can be reproduced, poked at, and shared with a link.
		</p>
		<p>
			The source is on <a href="https://github.com/davidsneighbour/tailwind-asylum">GitHub</a>.
		</p>
	</div>
</Layout>
